161-### Phase 18: Quantized KV Cache (Q8_0 and Q4_0 Paged/Continuous Cache)
162-- Priority: P1
163:- Status: COMPLETED
164-- Rationale: Storing KV activations in full FP32 consumes excessive RAM on large context lengths. Quantizing KV-cache vectors to Q8_0 or Q4_0 cuts KV memory footprint by 3.5x to 6.4x with near-zero perplexity impact.
165-- Files: `src/kv.rs`, `src/model.rs`, `src/lib.rs`, `src/main.rs`, `src/server.rs`, `tests/model.rs`
--
169-### Phase 19: Paged KV-Cache & Block Table Allocator
170-- Priority: P1
171:- Status: COMPLETED
172-- Rationale: Eliminates contiguous KV buffer pre-allocation and memory fragmentation by organizing KV cache into fixed-size physical blocks (e.g. 16 or 32 tokens) with logical-to-physical block tables (vLLM style).
173-- Files: `src/paged.rs`, `src/model.rs`, `src/lib.rs`, `tests/paged.rs`
